# civil-holidays-translations v1
# source: translation
# retrieved: 2026-07-22
# note:
#   DISPLAY translations, NOT official names. Every row here is a rendering we
#   authored for convenience - a way to *show* a holiday in another language -
#   and is deliberately kept distinct from the official native names that live
#   in the per-jurisdiction .tab files. The golden rule still holds: a holiday's
#   real name is what its own government calls it (that is the primary `name`
#   and any co-official `names`); these are only helpful glosses. The join key
#   is the holiday's PRIMARY name (its official native name) exactly as spelled
#   in the jurisdiction's .tab file. A language is omitted for a holiday when
#   that language is already its official name (carried in the .tab `names`).
# columns: jurisdiction | name | lang | text
#
